NVIDIA software
---------------

NVIDIA CUDA libraries (CUDA runtime, nvcc, cuBLAS, cuDNN, NCCL, NVSHMEM and related
packages) are proprietary NVIDIA software, used unmodified under the NVIDIA CUDA
Toolkit End User License Agreement (https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/).

On NVIDIA drivers 535 to 579, data-center GPUs use NVIDIA's CUDA forward
compatibility libraries, which come from NVIDIA under NVIDIA's license and are not
redistributed by Goethe.

